{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/75734-inspiration-for-werewolf-that-doesn-t-involve-werwolves","id":75734,"title":"Inspiration for Werewolf that doesn't involve werwolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-20T10:47:10-08:00","id":75734,"title":"Inspiration for Werewolf that doesn't involve werwolves","content":"I have a love/hate relationship with Werewolf (both versions). I love the shamanistic/animistic elements, and the pack mentality, I love the Pure in Forsaken, and I like some of the treibes in both versions but I hate the Werewolf aspect, or at least how it's typicialy played, where the rage and bestial nature of werewolves is constantly coming up to the point of tedium. I compare this to my experience eof Vampire where the Beast rare3ly shows and, thus, when it does, it packs more punch. A lot of this is personal experience and beside the point of the thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> Since I don't care for the Werewolf genre in general, I'm looking for good stories to get the feel of werewolf without the trappings of lycanthropy. I always find inspiration works better for me if it's not tied too directly.<br /> <br /> For example: for Vampire I look to Boardwalk Empire, for Hunter, Supernatural, and for Changeling, Black Swan.<br /> <br /> The closest I can come to something like that for werewolf is the Hell's Angels, and thus, Sons of Anarchy comes to mind, but while the Angels are a good example of a pack of Pure (or villainous Forsaken) I still more before I can really grok Werewolf.<br /> <br /> And before somebody brings up my rant at the beginning I will say that I can accept the wolf part of the game, i'd just emphasize Uratha as creatures of passion rather than overplaying the animalistic part.<br /> <br /> Thanks., and I don't mean to crap on your game by complaining about the central feature of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2336-alokov","name":"alokov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T11:31:48-08:00","id":75774,"title":"","content":"Some of the police/authorities shows are good for this, as well, since they do work in a group.<br /> <br /> Best examples I can think of right now:<br /> <br /> <b>Hawaii 5-O </b>(new version). Each member of the &quot;pack&quot; brings something different to the table. There is a clear alpha and beta dynamic between McGarrett and Dano. The inclusion of the SWAT team captain in the new season is a good example for conflicting packs.<br /> <br /> <b>Criminal Minds</b>. A &quot;pack&quot; of &quot;hunters&quot; who take the time to know they're &quot;prey&quot; before they even make a move. When they do move, it's precise and effective, and if it ends in bloodshed, it's because the &quot;prey&quot; was trapped and didn't know what else to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T14:05:42-08:00","id":75873,"title":"","content":"Any &quot;group of soldier&quot; fiction is a great place to start. When you get people working together in a unit, you have great fodder for how a pack can come together and face challenges that would be insurmountable to the individual. If you like to focus on the potential conflict within the pack, any &quot;group of misfits&quot; fiction is a great place to start.<br /> <br /> Farscape: The characters are already pretty much <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FiveManBand\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;five-man band&quot;</a> archetypes, which would be great fodder for a werewolf chronicle. Crichton is the Elodoth, Aeryn is the Rahu, D'argo is the Cahaliath, Zhann is the Ithaeur, Rygel is the Irraka.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T21:49:20-08:00","id":76094,"title":"","content":"There's this fantastic author, Charlee Jacob. What she writes is pretty much equivalent to the World of Darkness, and a particularly brutal take on it.<br /> The first book of hers I read was called 'This Symbiotic Fascination,' which is essentially about a Uratha without the wolf aspect. He's predatory, and a monster, but he's more of the Uratha, if you took the wolf part away but kept the heavy spiritual aspect. He's influenced by spirits around him, and the spirits of those he hurts, both physically (resulting in a sort of shapechange) and through other urges. There was an example of something like that in the chronicler's guide, the idea that if a werewolf hunts down certain types of spirits they can become like that kind of spirit, I remember an example of eating bulldozer spirits and getting kind of a broad forehead and yellowish tint to their skin. His mother was a more traditional werewolf, and would probably be the equivalent of a zi'ir or Pure. It runs in the family, as another of Jacob's books deal with the brother of this character, who in Cambodia loses focus and becomes claimed by the spirit of a powerful, ancient god.<br /> <br /> Great book, great author, but very dark and brutal at points, so it may not be your cup of tea, though I thought it was a very interesting take on werewolves, and there's a novel take on vampires in it too.<br /> <br /> Also since ErikModi mentioned Farscape, which was indeed a great show, I have to suggest Blake's 7, a strong inspiration for Farscape. The effects are dated, but it's about a band of imperfect people trying to do some good in a world that seems like it may never change. Along the way, old allies die and new allies arrive and ancient secrets and strangers are unearthed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-21-2014, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T11:53:33-08:00","id":82193,"title":"","content":"Maybe it won't help for the Uratha themselves but I've drawn heavy inspiration for the Shadow from the Gonzo art of Ralph Steadman. If you're having trouble coming up with what the Hisil looks like then Steadman's art should help give form to the ephemeral madness and subversive decay Werewolf needs to hit home that the Shadow isn't nice. The writing and writer that created Gonzo, Hunter S. Thompson, can be used as well, to a certain degree. I feel like Fear and Loathing in Las Vegas works best for Promethean honestly, what with the point of the book being the search for the American Dream, but HST's frantic and mad writing style shows what it's like to have your brain on fire, which I feel works great for the Forsaken. <br /> <br /> Obvious and very much out of tone with WtF, I still feel that the Incredible Hulk can be looked at for inspiration. Whether you want to show how a man of peace deals with a heart of destruction a la Mark Ruffalo in the Avengers or go on ridiculous battle adventures fighting your red counterparts (I mean I wouldn't but Red Hulk apparently sells so...) Bruce Banner and his gama irradiated allies and enemies can be looked at for Werewolf stories. If nothing else at least you can use them as examples of how cool it looks when really big monster people try to kill each other.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But that would be *shudders* <i>fun</i>!<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/119-strapping-gent","name":"Strapping Gent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T12:08:35-08:00","id":82202,"title":"","content":"<b>The Shield </b>is hands own my favourite Werewolf inspiration - they are cops with a distinctly predatory edge to them, using every means necessary to ensure their territory's stability. Pack business is kept within the pack and outsiders arenot welcome (though I could see them as a Pure pack)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T14:59:43-08:00","id":82331,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Ocean's 11&quot; series of films. Effective pack dynamics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","